# Keeps build context small and, more importantly, keeps secrets and local state
# out of the image. `.env` is listed first because it is the one that matters:
# a committed .dockerignore is the last thing standing between a developer's
# local credentials and a published image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/.vite

.git
.github
docs
**/*.md
!README.md

# Generated Prisma client: regenerated inside the image for the target platform.
apps/api/src/generated

# Local database volume and anything else Docker Compose leaves behind.
.docker
docker-compose.yml

**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
